From: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Stop reception before unloading SDR++ modules

Let the source close the USB receiver during normal application shutdown.

Base: SDR++ 8c9f5ee8fe405775bfcd62c8c8f8c0fc928a64af
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

diff --git a/core/src/core.cpp b/core/src/core.cpp
--- a/core/src/core.cpp
+++ b/core/src/core.cpp
@@ -404,6 +404,9 @@ int sdrpp_main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
-
+
     // On android, none of this shutdown should happen due to the way the UI works
 #ifndef __ANDROID__
+    // Stop the active source before unloading modules so device cleanup runs.
+    gui::mainWindow.setPlayState(false);
+
     // Shut down all modules
     for (auto& [name, mod] : core::moduleManager.modules) {
         mod.end();
